msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:42
#: c2315d3225f64260b37bbc508bde3094
msgid "The default RC input is configured on the UART2_RX inverted from the SBUS pin.  All unidirectional ArduPilot compatible protocols, except PPM, are supported. Receivers using bi-directional protocols such as CRSF/ELRS should be tied to the TX2 and RX2 pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:44
#: 0cb2bd02c8eb43d982b3922ad6f5c7bb
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX2 . See :ref:`FPort Receivers<common-Fport-receivers>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:45
#: 6787c1fcb21a4eacaaaa1154d2241859
msgid "CRSF/ELRS also requires a TX2 connection, in addition to RX2, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:46
#: 74ee4680412049099066df9696eb9532
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX2 and automatically provides telemetry. Set :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` to “4”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:49
#: edb26134932f42aaaf74cfc7503c6211
msgid "FrSky Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:50
#: a63bb1d1e5ad4ef59e7df7a7d2e65489
msgid "FrSky Telemetry can be supported using any UART. For example, the T4 pin (UART4 transmit). You need to set the following parameters to enable support for FrSky S.PORT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:52
#: 376874d151344e588f46c1d0db5569fe
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL<SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:53
#: 6357dd26d7064bf5879cfcd470d63a75
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS<SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:56
#: 0b533ead3dee42a1bdc066269be3d031
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:57
#: d669b4dff9134602894da88cbb260df9
msgid "The BROTHERHOBBYH743 supports using its internal OSD (MAX7456 driver). Simultaneous DisplayPort OSD operation  is also pre-configured on SERIAL 6. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:60
#: 54315748c93b4e529dbd8380d99eda90
msgid "VTX Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:61
#: b8392f9a17d94e5898d45aa4df52ede1
msgid "The SH1.0-6P connector supports a standard DJI HD VTX connection. Pin 1 of the connector is 12v so be careful not to connect to devices that cannot accept that voltage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:64
#: 0f868749433f470e8db9df2947291905
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:65
#: add3bac6a2494cb8a8b00e07ccb70fb8
msgid "The BROTHERHOBBYH743 supports up to 13 PWM outputs. All outputs except 11/12 support DShot. Outputs 1-8 support bi-directional DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:67
#: 7b69a6711f54484e89f280f1e53fd8c0
msgid "PWM outputs are grouped and every group must use the same output protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:69
#: 8b293b369ddd4d0f9dd8d425f9641763
msgid "PWM 1-2   in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:70
#: 4d556f07de4b413f986b85f20c66bbcb
msgid "PWM 3-4   in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:71
#: 7de3cf8b0df64d82a763976527cc256c
msgid "PWM 5-6   in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:72
#: 86bfb909baaf4ed8b69aa0f104250e7f
msgid "PWM 7-10  in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:73
#: 5a35d03dc7cd4206b0aaa7e1ea8cb3ef
msgid "PWM 11-12 in group5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:74
#: 6cdee13affa74368984c144fb7bfb2e2
msgid "PWM 13    in group6 - LED strip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:77
#: 8d4aa8a12fa6424e98c7245fc7e6aa4d
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:78
#: 04b71a038afd4ab5bd0c935dc3851603
msgid "The board has a internal voltage sensor and connections on the ESC connector for an external current sensor input. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:80
#: e8ab16ab42bf40c6a2aae999093a21c8
msgid "The default battery parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:82
#: 5739545989e749de8a3212201fe77035
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:83
#: 425ce5f957fb40e9a0dcc335e61b1a9c
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN <BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:84
#: 27f358838fd347429d8b2b9d7beacea9
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN <BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:85
#: a25e2d07836d472c81e9da851c7404a8
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT <BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:86
#: 16f96fc75f9f4a9db757c2a1ae41abfc
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT <BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 40.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:89
#: b6d5cf6ad8b44fc7a5e0336887a89880
msgid "RSSI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:90
#: cef7a71d7fb74d228c3f2bcb43518b28
msgid "ADC Pin 8 -> RSSI voltage monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:93
#: eee9d8bc1f1b46f6ac371505bdf65ae1
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:94
#: 2636a02b48f245f8bc8b5bf8d0ae245b
msgid "The BROTHERHOBBYH743 does not have a built-in compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:97
#: af8bfb805a12463487aa458f934eda32
msgid "VTX power control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:98
#: 5d04c16507704417bbd61082a63b70cb
msgid "GPIO 81 controls the VTX BEC output to pins marked \"10V\". Setting this GPIO low removes voltage supply to pins. By default RELAY2 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:101
#: 000fdde8065f4996ab2a15a366e0b359
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:102
#: 768a567cd4e246398a4964350e74e799
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the camera output to the connectors marked \"CAM1\" and \"CAM2\". Setting this GPIO high switches the video output from CAM1 to CAM2. By default RELAY3 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO low."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:105
#: 4a71f5bcecbd47fb880940b8a00be0c8
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:106
#: 1a45afce5e4a4cc3ad42af7fe38c5d66
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favorite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:108
#: e681252c85814e0d9c94fabb286b7330
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \"\\*.apj\" firmware files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brotherhobbyh743.rst:110
#: c9f1a9c7b72e4a24bb3f746b05e0106e
msgid "Firmware for these boards can be found at https://firmware.ardupilot.org in sub-folders labeled \"BROTHEHOBBYH743\"."
msgstr ""
